From 0c6fe66de4effbbd5a7e2e52a4e633b9d811d721 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:35:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu-bridge: Fix the link frequencies of the ov13858

The entry added for the Surface Pro 9 rear camera passes the number of
CSI-2 lanes (4) as the number of link frequencies, while only one
frequency is listed and the table has room for three. The bridge then
copies four values into the "link-frequencies" endpoint property,
reading past the end of the entry into the next one.

List the two link frequencies the ov13858 driver supports instead
(540 MHz for the full resolution modes, 270 MHz for the binned ones).
The Surface Pro 8 uses the same rear camera module (OVTID858).

Patchset: cameras
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
index e930f39e6..044a21eb3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -64,8 +64,8 @@ static const struct ipu_sensor_config ipu_supported_sensors[] = {
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT33F0", 1, 384000000),
 	/* Omnivision OV5693 - Surface Pro 9 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("OVTI5693", 1, 419200000),
-	/* Omnivision OV13858 - Surface Pro 9 */
-	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("OVTID858", 4, 540000000),
+	/* Omnivision OV13858 - Surface Pro 8, Pro 9 */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("OVTID858", 2, 540000000, 270000000),
 	/* Omnivision OV2740 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT3474", 1, 180000000),
 	/* Omnivision OV5670 */
-- 
